  "details": "# Feature:\n\n**The ability the set a \"priority\" number on physbones.**\n\n# Applications:\n\n***Quest Limits***\n\nI originally thought of this feature as a way to prevent Quest avatars from having *all* their physbones removed if you go over the Quest limit. The idea is that it can remove the last `n-limit` physbones, but keep the rest under the limit.\n\n***Safety/Performance Settings***\n\nHowever, I realized this could double as a way to set physbone limits in dense instances.\n\nTo my understanding, physbones scale very well. Nearly to the point that each avatar could have 100 components of 8 transforms each in an 80 person instance and *still probably run just fine*. \n\nThis could double as a way for a user to define which physbones are \"important\" and in what order. This way, other users can toggle a \"limiter\" for dense instances, or non-friends, or even based on distance. Priority could be super helpful for enabling both *very* complex avatar interactions, as well as to properly manage performance.",
